WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.710
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"
is almost in theaters, but what should fans

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.050
expect from a Sam Raimi/MCU collab?

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.010
And who is "America Chavez"?

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.269
These questions and more, answered, straight
ahead.

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:20.699
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"
premieres in theaters on May 6, 2022.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:24.740
Marvel head honcho Kevin Feige had initially
announced that the sequel was set to release

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:30.220
a year earlier, but it ended up getting delayed
due to reshoots and other production issues,

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.430
in addition to COVID-19 interruptions.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:37.340
"Thor: Love and Thunder" and other upcoming
Phase Four titles were also pushed back due

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.610
to the COVID pandemic, but "Multiverse of
Madness" had other setbacks, including a change

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.610
in filmmakers.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:48.640
In fact, one source told the Hollywood Reporter
that new director Sam Raimi and new writer

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.960
Michael Waldron were brought on to essentially
"create a whole new movie."

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.420
While MCU fans have been getting impatient
for the new Doctor Strange vehicle, those

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.420
who enjoy the darker side of cinema will likely
be happier with the end result, as Raimi and

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.789
Waldron reportedly used their delayed timetable
to make the movie just a little bit more scary.

00:01:08.789 --> 00:01:13.789
Sam Raimi is no stranger to either superheroes
or horror — his previous work includes the

00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:19.590
original "Spider-Man" trilogy, the "Evil Dead"
trilogy, and many other horror films and comic-inspired

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.079
projects.

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:25.610
In a 2022 Empire interview, Kevin Feige explained
that when searching for a director, their

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:30.770
team thought scoring Raimi would be "incredible,"
but didn't think there was any chance of it

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:31.770
happening.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.540
However, Raimi ultimately agreed to set up
a meeting and the enthusiasm he had for the

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:39.060
project made the choice a no-brainer on both
sides.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.469
Horror filmmaker Scott Derrickson, who directed
the first "Doctor Strange" film, was originally

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:47.799
going to return for the sequel before leaving
in January 2020.

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:49.029
Feige told Empire,

00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:52.170
"We love Scott and I think Scott feels the
same.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.579
Nobody believes it, but it was just creative
differences."

00:01:55.579 --> 00:02:00.619
Neither Marvel nor Derrickson himself seem
to harbor any ill will around this decision,

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:05.039
and both appear excited to see the project
come together with Raimi in the director's

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:06.039
chair.

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:10.110
There are many theories as to what might be
behind the problems with the multiverse in

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.890
the new "Doctor Strange" film.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:16.750
The ending of Marvel's first Disney+ series,
"WandaVision," which sees Wanda Maximoff use

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.880
chaos magic to inadvertently rewrite reality,
revealed that Wanda's powers surpass those

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.100
of the Sorcerer Supreme, and that it is her
destiny to destroy the world.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:31.200
Kevin Feige confirmed at the 2019 Comic-Con
panel that the events of "WandaVision" would

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.290
tie directly into the new "Doctor Strange"
project, and the trailers confirm it.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.510
"I made mistakes, and people were hurt."

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.130
"I'm not here to talk about Westview."

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:47.460
But then there's "Loki," another Disney+ show
in which the protagonists' climactic confrontation

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:52.460
with "He Who Remains," aka Kang, results in
new branches of reality splitting from the

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.390
primary timeline, potentially allowing the
multiverse to take shape.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:01.150
And of course, there's Doctor Strange himself,
who makes several ill-advised decisions in

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.820
"Spider-Man: No Way Home," beginning with
a spell that accidentally summons both interdimensional

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.290
villains and various Peter Parkers.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:13.350
The movie ends with another spell that makes
everyone forget Spider-Man's secret identity.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:18.010
Strange mind-wiping the entire human race
seems likely to have a dangerous outcome,

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:22.160
and the trailers for "Multiverse of Madness"
certainly seem to indicate that he's directly

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.460
responsible for, at the very least, opening
the doorway between universes.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:30.230
"Things just got out of hand."

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:34.360
With Wanda Maximoff having officially gained
the moniker of the Scarlet Witch, fans have

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.540
been eagerly awaiting the return of Elizabeth
Olsen to Marvel's big screen.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.250
Olsen was among a small group of stars that
were the first to confirm their involvement

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.870
in the "Doctor Strange" sequel, leading to
heaps of speculation as to what her part in

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.670
this story would be.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:52.320
Most importantly, would Wanda be among the
film's heroes ... or its villain?

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.570
The Scarlet Witch wields immense power, but
has been given very little knowledge on how

00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:00.920
to apply it — though by the end of "WandaVision,"
she certainly seems to be learning.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:06.120
She has also suffered immense loss, both before
and during the mental breakdown that culminated

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.790
in the creation of the Hex, and her puppeting
of the people of Westview wasn't exactly the

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.319
most morally upstanding of actions.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:18.000
Wanda's chaos magic is the stuff of myth and
legend, a degree of power that could potentially

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.959
destroy her own reality, and possibly others.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:25.010
She certainly appears to be on the side of
the angels in the "Multiverse of Madness"

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.510
trailer, but there are also numerous hints
that she might not stay there.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:33.191
Hopefully this won't be Wanda's final descent
into darkness, but if it is, at least we get

00:04:33.191 --> 00:04:35.480
to see Olsen go full evil.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:41.540
Xochitl Gomez makes her Marvel debut as America
Chavez in "Multiverse of Madness," and while

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:46.889
we might not know much about her exact role
in the MCU, we do have some significant background

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:50.010
information on her character from the comics.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:55.150
America boasts superhuman strength, speed,
and durability, as well as flight, but her

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:59.850
signature power is the ability to open star-shaped
portals that allow her to travel instantly

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:05.030
across the multiverse, which makes sense considering
the movie in which she's being introduced.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:09.320
She's been a member of various incarnations
of the Avengers as well as other teams like

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.760
the Ultimates.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.330
America originally believed herself to have
been born in an extradimensional paradise

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:19.540
called the Utopian Parallel, which was responsible
for giving her superpowers and which her mothers

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.790
sacrificed themselves to save.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:25.980
Recently, however, this story has been called
into question with the appearance of America's

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:31.380
previously unknown sister, who told America
that the Utopian Parallel was actually a private

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:36.470
island research facility on Earth, and America's
powers are actually the result of genetic

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:37.470
experimentation.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:41.960
"Multiverse of Madness" will likely go with
the better-known version of the backstory,

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.280
but you never know.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:49.300
Regardless, America brings some much-needed
LGBTQ+ representation to the MCU, as she is

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:54.740
a lesbian and appears to be sporting a gay
pride pin on her costume in the trailers.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:58.139
In the "Official Trailer" for "Multiverse
of Madness," fans were quick to recognize

00:05:58.139 --> 00:06:03.740
a familiar voice: that of Patrick Stewart,
who played Professor Charles Xavier in 20th

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:05.980
Century Fox's "X-Men" film franchise.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.210
"We should tell him the truth."

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:12.790
As the founder of the X-Men, a comic book
property recently reclaimed by Marvel Studios,

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:17.830
Xavier's presence would be explicit confirmation
that mutants have finally made their way to

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:23.389
the MCU, and what better way to explain their
arrival than with multiversal shenanigans?

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:27.240
Stewart himself has been careful with his
words when asked about the upcoming Marvel

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.240
project.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.240
He told Rolling Stone,

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.300
"All I can say to you is we'll have to see.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.710
But bear in mind that Professor Xavier has
already died twice."

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:38.860
Of course, it seems likely that Stewart would
be playing an alternate universe version of

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.490
the character, rendering those other deaths
moot.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:46.090
In a recent interview with Jake Hamilton,
however, Stewart seemed to confirm his involvement

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.770
in the upcoming movie.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.530
Discussing the trailer, Stewart said,

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:51.919
"I actually didn't recognize my own voice.

00:06:51.919 --> 00:06:53.449
It sounded different.

00:06:53.449 --> 00:06:56.180
Whether I had a cold or something at the time,
I don't know."

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.040
He also recalled being "astonished" that fans
would realize it was him.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:03.889
That certainly makes it sound like Stewart
is in the movie, for sure — whether he's

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:09.360
actually reprising his role as the mutant
master of telepathy remains to be seen.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:15.120
In March 2019, after Disney acquired 21st
Century Fox, Marvel Studios obtained the film

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.310
rights to the X-Men as well as the Fantastic
Four.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:23.070
Neither have yet been integrated into the
MCU, but if Patrick Stewart really is returning

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:28.600
as Charles Xavier, the door for the mutants'
arrival has potentially been kicked wide open,

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:30.870
leading to all sorts of possibilities.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:35.210
Eagle-eyed fans were also quick to point out
a possible Easter egg related to Ryan Reynolds'

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:39.580
Deadpool in the newest promotional poster
for "Multiverse of Madness."

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:43.520
Among the shards of glass surrounding Doctor
Strange, there is one that contains what looks

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.120
like Deadpool doing his iconic "shush" pose.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:50.290
While this might just be the Marvel team's
way of having some fun with the idea of the

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.830
multiverse, this theory actually holds some
weight.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:57.520
In 2021, Kevin Feige made headlines when he
confirmed that the next Deadpool film will

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.950
be part of the MCU.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.580
"Wade, you are better than this.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.960
Join us.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.850
Use your powers for good."

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:06.850
"Heads up."

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.330
"Be a superhero."

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:12.350
In a brief shot during the "Multiverse of
Madness" trailer, Doctor Strange is handcuffed

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:15.699
and escorted to a room by Ultron-style robots.

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:20.470
Once he reaches this room, there's a council
of six individuals seated before him.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:24.620
This is when viewers heard the voice of Patrick
Stewart and instantly connected the dots on

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.830
what this group likely is: the Illuminati.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:31.830
In the comics, the Illuminati is a secret
organization made up of some of the most intelligent

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:34.820
and powerful individuals in the Marvel Universe.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:40.750
The original group was comprised of Tony Stark,
Charles Xavier, Reed Richards, Stephen Strange,

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:45.710
Black Bolt, and Namor, but the roster has
changed occasionally over the years.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:50.410
Regardless, the members of the Illuminati
act as unelected overseers of the superhuman

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:55.450
world, sharing ideas and strategy on how to
govern super-powered people, despite their

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.890
conflicting aspirations.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:01.750
If, as punishment for his "desecration of
reality," Doctor Strange really is being brought

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.920
before the Illuminati, it opens up vast new
worlds of possibility.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.160
Who else will be a part of this organization?

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.280
Could we finally be getting an introduction
to the MCU's Reed Richards?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:15.860
Could we be getting Namor, or another version
of Tony Stark who's still alive?

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.430
What role will the Illuminati play in the
future of the MCU — the second season of

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:21.430
"Loki," for example?

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:26.220
And most importantly, would even "Multiverse
of Madness" dare to reference the ill-fated

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.200
"Inhumans" show?

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.990
If we've learned anything from "Spider-Man:
No Way Home" and "Loki," it's that it can

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:35.970
be quite disorienting to come face-to-face
with another version of yourself.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:39.800
The newest trailer for "Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness," seem to confirm

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:43.120
the inclusion of many variants of our lead
protagonist.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:47.260
Sinister Strange will most likely prove to
be an adversary to our prime Strange, and

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:50.750
looks somewhat reminiscent of the Strange
Supreme of "What If…?"

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:51.750
episode 4.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.800
Defender Strange is seen with striped hair
pulled back into a ponytail and appears to

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:59.050
be working alongside America Chavez as a protector.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:03.780
Finally, Zombie Strange appears as an undead
version of the superhero, strikingly similar

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:07.160
to the same character from Disney+ series,
"What If...?"

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:11.570
There's also at least one alternate version
of Wanda, shown confronting her other self

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:14.340
in what appears to be their wrecked Westview
home.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:18.310
This could be a sign of Wanda's consciousness
breaking into two following the traumatic

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:22.310
events of "WandaVision," but a variant is
probably more likely.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:26.100
The fact that there's a version of Wanda in
street clothes confronting the fully-costumed

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:31.040
Scarlet Witch suggests the possibility of
there being an evil version of our Wanda,

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.140
possibly one that was corrupted by the Darkhold.

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:39.230
The end of "WandaVision" saw Wanda Maximoff
finally take her place as the Scarlet Witch,

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:41.670
complete with iconic red suit and magic powers.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:46.040
However, throughout the "Multiverse of Madness"
trailer, there are several changes made to

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.890
her costume that are hard to miss.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.290
Her red suit appears to be growing darker,
bordering on black.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:55.200
Her sleeves have now completely covered her
arms and there seems to be black at the tips

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:59.830
of her fingers, similar to Agatha Harkness
when she used dark magic in "WandaVision."

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:04.940
Are these changes merely aesthetic, or could
they symbolize her upcoming descent into darkness?

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:10.040
It should also be noted that in the comics,
Wanda is a "Nexus being" — individuals described

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:15.120
as "keystones of the Multiverse," with the
ability to affect probability and the future.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:19.910
This concept hasn't yet been fully introduced
to the MCU, but there have been some important

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.140
hints:

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:26.089
"Nexus: Because the world doesn't revolve
around you.

00:11:26.089 --> 00:11:27.580
Or does it?"

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.370
There's a lot we don't know, but it's clear
that the Scarlet Witch is, at the very least,

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.240
going to be an important player in the "Multiverse
of Madness."

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:39.930
It's the overarching question hanging above
"Multiverse of Madness": Who is the ultimate

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:41.240
villain of the story?

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:45.720
Wanda Maximoff herself, or a variant of her,
is the obvious answer, but there definitely

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.339
seems to be at least one evil Doctor Strange
in the trailer.

00:11:49.339 --> 00:11:53.779
There's also Kang the Conqueror, of course,
who invented the Time Variance Authority in

00:11:53.779 --> 00:11:57.850
order to maintain the "proper" flow of the
Sacred Timeline, and who promised that other

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:01.710
versions of himself would invade the multiverse
after his death.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:06.120
Another possibility is Chthon, the original
author of the Darkhold in the comics, who

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.510
also has a comic book connection to the Scarlet
Witch.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:13.399
And then there's Nightmare, the original Doctor
Strange villain, who rules the Nightmare Realm

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:15.560
and feeds off the fear of mortal sleepers.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:20.459
In the trailer, Doctor Strange says that he
is having the same dream every night, and

00:12:20.459 --> 00:12:24.620
original director Scott Derrickson was very
interested in including Nightmare in the story

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.160
going forward.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.410
Despite rewrites and reshoots, it's possible
that Sam Raimi kept Nightmare as the central

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.750
villain when he took over on "Multiverse of
Madness."

